{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["And it was when Pharaoh stubbornly refused — all this you shall say to your son, and so Scripture proves by writing ״HaShem brought us out of Egypt״ — for the Holy One, blessed be He, said this entire passage to Moshe. And Israel says to his son: ״HaShem brought us out,״ etc. — for Moshe did not say this verse to Israel on his own initiative, that Moshe would say to Israel: ״And it shall be for a sign upon your hand, for with strength of hand HaShem brought us out,״ etc. — rather, the father says thus to his son."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {0 "The lemma is an abbreviated citation of Exodus 13:15; the full verse begins ויהי כי הקשה פרעה. The phrase על ידכה reflects the cited verse's singular form."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:41:23.661153861Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}